  "legal": {
   "import_restricted": [
    "European Union - not blocked, but EU units ship firmware with the deauthentication feature removed, which the vendor attributes to Radio Equipment Directive rules effective 1 August 2025"
   ],
   "risk_level": "medium",
   "notes": "This is one of the very few devices in this class with a proper compliance paper trail: FCC Grant of Equipment Authorization and SDoC, Canadian ICES-003, CE RED/EMC/RoHS, UKCA plus a UK PSTI statement, Australian/NZ RCM, and a published security-support commitment through 30 September 2027. Owning it is legal. Using the deauther against networks you do not own is a separate offence in most countries, which is precisely why the EU build ships without it. Channels 13 and 14 are restricted in some regions."
  },
