   "notes": "This board combines an amplified sub-GHz transmitter, an amplified 2.4GHz module and NFC in one device, which puts it in a different regulatory category from a plain ESP32 board. Transmitting on sub-GHz without a licence, exceeding local power limits with the PA, and deliberately interfering with 2.4GHz are separate offences in most countries, on top of the usual computer-misuse exposure from deauth and credential portals. Owning it is generally fine; several of its transmit features are not something you can lawfully test outside a shielded environment. Check your local law."
