   "mifare_classic_attacks": {
    "v": "partial",
    "note": "Best-in-class for a device this cheap, but know the boundary. On device: dictionary attack against known keys, and the mfkey32 READER attack (emulate the card at a real reader, harvest nonces, recover Crypto-1 keys in a few minutes). Community firmware also adds card-only nested attack collection. What still generally needs a PC is the heavy maths: hardnested and full nested recovery, where the Flipper collects nonces into a .nested.log and a desktop tool or web service does the cracking. Static nested can be finished on device. Once keys are known it emulates the card and can write to 'magic' cards."
   },
   "nfc_type4_ndef": {
    "v": "yes",
    "note": "This is a genuine community-firmware-only capability. The forks add Type4Tag and Ntag4xx protocol modules that official firmware does not have: they READ NTAG 4xx and generic ISO14443-4 Type 4 tags, and there is a Type4Tag LISTENER, so the Flipper can present itself as an NDEF Type 4 tag (this is what the NFC Maker app uses to serve URLs, Wi-Fi credentials, contact cards). Note Ntag4xx itself is read-only - its listener entry is NULL - and DESFire emulation does not exist on any firmware."
   },
   "emv_read": {
    "v": "partial",
    "note": "Community firmware has a real EMV poller, so it can read the openly-readable side of a contactless bank card: PAN, expiry, cardholder name where present, and sometimes a transaction log. That is NOT cloning - it cannot produce the dynamic cryptogram a terminal demands, so it cannot pay. Worth knowing: the EMV plugin was silently BROKEN for a long stretch - it shipped as a plugin that never loaded at all - and was only fixed in Unleashed PR #1073, merged 2026-08-20, then flowed downstream. If you used a build from before late August 2026, EMV appeared to be supported but did nothing."
   },
   "hf_1356_emulate": {
    "v": "partial",
    "note": "Emulation exists for ISO14443-3A, ISO14443-4A, ISO15693-3, MIFARE Ultralight, MIFARE Classic, MIFARE Plus, SLIX, FeliCa and generic Type 4 Tag. Still NULL and therefore impossible: ISO14443-3B, ISO14443-4B, DESFire, ST25TB, NTAG4xx."
   },
