   "notes": "The board itself is three common radio modules; we found no import restrictions on the category. The risk is in use. Deauthentication frames and rogue access points against networks you do not own are computer-misuse offences in most countries and unlawful interference under FCC rules in the US. The 'nRF24 jammer' apps that circulate for these boards deliberately transmit to disrupt other users' equipment, which is a specific offence in the US (47 U.S.C. 333) and its equivalents elsewhere regardless of how low the power is. Sub-GHz transmission has separate regional limits. Owning the board is not the issue."
