   "risk_level": "high",
   "notes": "Owning and receiving with a HackRF is legal in most countries, and listening across the spectrum is generally unrestricted in the US (with the notable exception of intercepting cellular voice). Transmitting is a completely different matter: HackRF can transmit on aviation, emergency services, cellular and satellite bands, and doing so without a licence is a criminal offence in nearly every jurisdiction. In the US that is FCC Part 15/301 territory and can carry very large fines. Even a low-power test transmission should go into a shielded enclosure or a dummy load, not an antenna. Check your local regulator before you key up."
