   "notes": "The hardware is a coil and an H-bridge and is not itself restricted. The use is the problem: in the US, possessing or using a device to encode or replay payment card data with intent to defraud is charged under 18 U.S.C. 1029 (access device fraud), and most states have separate skimming statutes; equivalent offences exist across the EU and UK. Replaying access badges you are not authorised to use is trespass or burglary depending on jurisdiction. Rabbit-Labs' own listing states it is for educational, research and personal use. Use only on cards and readers you own or are contracted to test, and keep the authorisation in writing."
