  "honest_take": "This is the answer to 'what should I actually buy to sniff BLE', and almost nobody knows it. Watching all three advertising channels at once is not a nice-to-have - it is the difference between catching the connection request and missing it, and Sniffle's own documentation puts connection detection at roughly three times more reliable than single-channel sniffers. It beats a retired $125 Ubertooth and a $11 Nordic dongle on capability while sitting between them on price. The catches are real but small: you must flash it yourself, doing so removes the Zigbee function, and Sniffle is a link-layer capture tool - it does not break encryption, and a connection using LE Secure Connections pairing will be captured but not readable.",
